Track 3: "Who Cleared the Pressure Hatch at Slack Water?"
- Story & Context: Following the sudden decommissioning of the Valentia Island telegraph station in the spring of 1979, nocturnal trespassers broke into the flooded basement generator vault to find the high-voltage pumps still idling to a steady sixty-cycle hum. Scene founder Donald MacIntyre rigged three space echo units to the station's copper grounding rods, capturing the tide surging through the intake pipes while Rhys's harpsichord rolled through towering, feedback-drenched post-rock crescendos that rattled the slate roofs of the village. As the spring tide peaked, an unidentified voice on the coastguard VHF channel broke squelch with the chilling inquiry: "who cleared the pressure hatch at slack water when the diver never surfaced?" The recording was pressed in a limited run of two hundred unlabelled 12-inch acetates, each hand-stamped with dried sea salt and sold exclusively out of maritime pub basements along the Kerry coast.
